### flyverse_plugin ###
# `mix.lock` and `Cargo.lock` are committed, because an example that resolves
# differently every time it is opened is one that stops working quietly, and the
# trees they resolve into are not. The Rust template ignores every `Cargo.lock`;
# this crate's is the one that says which flyverse revision the engine is.
!native/*/Cargo.lock

# The compiled engine belongs to the machine that built it. `mix compile` builds
# it (`mix flyverse_plugin.engine`), which is also why a clone or a `git clean`
# has to build rather than fetch it — a node whose library is missing raises
# `function FlyversePlugin.Native.open/1 is undefined` and offers nothing.
/priv/native/

